# Phosphor -- a monochrome terminal, and nothing else
#
# A P1 phosphor tube had one gun and one colour, and everything on it was
# told apart by brightness. So this collapses every hue almost entirely
# onto green -- but only almost, and it keeps each family's brightness
# exactly where it was. A red dragon still reads differently from a blue
# one; it just reads by weight rather than by hue, the way it did in 1974.

name    Phosphor
blurb   One green gun, and a bit of glow. 1974.

# --- interface roles -------------------------------------------------------
ui      canvas      030A04
ui      panel       07160A
ui      border      1F4A26
ui      title       9CFF7A
ui      text        6BE05A
ui      muted       2F7A38
ui      accent      C6FF9E
ui      selection   164A1E  D0

